{"id":"ass-donkey","name":"Ass (Donkey)","aliases":["Ass"],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ass-donkey"],"groups":["Domesticated"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ass","text":"Frequently mentioned throughout Scripture. Of the domesticated species we read of, (1.) The she ass (Heb. ‘athon), so named from its slowness (Gen. 12:16; 45:23; Num. 22:23; 1 Sam. 9:3). (2.) The male ass (Heb. hamor), the common working ass of Western Asia, so called from its red colour. Issachar is compared to a strong ass (Gen. 49:14). It was forbidden to yoke together an ass and an ox in the plough (Deut. 22:10). (3.) The ass’s colt (Heb. ‘air), mentioned Judg. 10:4; 12:14. It is rendered “foal” in Gen. 32:15; 49:11. (Comp. Job 11:12; Isa. 30:6.) The ass is an unclean animal, because it does not chew the cud (Lev. 11:26. Comp. 2 Kings 6:25). Asses constituted a considerable portion of wealth in ancient times (Gen. 12:16; 30:43; 1 Chr. 27:30; Job 1:3; 42:12). They were noted for their spirit and their attachment to their master (Isa. 1:3). They are frequently spoken of as having been …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2543","lemma":"חֲמוֹר","xlit":"chămôwr","gloss":"a male ass","kjv":"ass","count":26,"share":0.47},{"strong":"H860","lemma":"אָתוֹן","xlit":"ʼâthôwn","gloss":"a female donkey","kjv":"ass","count":13,"share":0.24},{"strong":"H6501","lemma":"פֶּרֶא","xlit":"pereʼ","gloss":"the onager","kjv":"wild","count":8,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H1109","lemma":"בִּלְעָם","xlit":"Bilʻâm","gloss":"Bilam, a Mesopotamian prophet","kjv":"Balaam, Bileam","count":8,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H1581","lemma":"גָּמָל","xlit":"gâmâl","gloss":"a camel","kjv":"camel","count":7,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H4397","lemma":"מֲלְאָךְ","xlit":"mălʼâk","gloss":"a messenger","kjv":"ambassador, angel, king, messenger","count":8,"share":0.15}],"verses":["Gen.12.16","Gen.22.3","Gen.24.35","Gen.32.5","Gen.34.28","Gen.42.26","Exod.13.13","Exod.23.12","Exod.34.20","Num.31.34","Num.31.45","Deut.22.10","Josh.15.18","